{field-5}} |  |  | {{field-6}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of equations that takes the following standard form:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $a(t),$ $b(t),$ $c(t),$ $d(t),$ $f(t),$ and $g(t)$ are known functions, and\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are unknown functions (dependent variables).\n\nSuch a system can always be written in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}a(t) & b(t) \\\\ c(t) & d(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ g(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have the following system.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)-2t\\,{x}_{1}(t)-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,{x}_{2}(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)+5{x}_{1}(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2t\\,{x}_{1}(t)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,{x}_{2}(t)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-5{x}_{1}(t)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can rewrite our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2t & 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304064 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6dfdbdba-247c-5ddd-bb6e-5d9637140264" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Linear System of Differential Equations in Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0ee46d0-6a9e-5b6f-852b-1280aa8fb3fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304066}] :answer-field/correct {:answ