, and\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are unknown functions (dependent variables).\n\nSuch a system can always be written in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}a(t) & b(t) \\\\ c(t) & d(t)\\end{aligned}],\\,f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}f(t) \\\\ g(t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have the following system.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)+{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t)=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{2}(t)+{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can rewrite our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304077 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6dfdbdba-247c-5ddd-bb6e-5d9637140264" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Linear System of Differential Equations in Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72b1cd24-4e82-5af4-90f5-30e62a7d494a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304079} {:answer/id #uuid "c6c33a53-374c-539f-84e0-dc254eaa2b4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72b1cd24-4e82-5af4-90f5-30e62a7d494a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304079} :answer-field/id #uuid "25e110df-8a20-57a9-b8cf-5313073f282f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304078} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8b45a85-0f64-5d98-939c-165c3921694b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304082}] :a